<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#processType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Classification of this ritual process. Values from ProcessTypeScheme. Access: public-unrestricted."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#CeremonialSequence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#initiationLevel-warriors> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#InitiationLevelScheme> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#role-initiant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The person receiving initiation or the primary recipient of the ceremony."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#processType-funerary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Death and funeral ceremonies specific to initiated practitioners. Includes ituto (Lucumi), axexe (Candomble), and rites handling spiritual obligations of deceased initiates."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#role-lead-officiant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Lead Officiant"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#TimingRequirementScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#timing-calendar-feast> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#authority-elder-designation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Requires recognition as an elder or authority holder within the tradition, beyond basic initiation. Community recognition is required in addition to initiation level."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#InitiationLevelScheme> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme> .
